# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches a *directory* and does not
# match a *symlink to* one — and every agent working in a `git worktree` symlinks this
# path back to the main checkout, because a worktree does not get its own install. So the
# symlink was not ignored, `git add -A` swept it up, and a mode-120000 blob whose contents
# are an absolute path on one machine got committed to a branch. Twice today, by two
# different agents, one of whom had already removed it once.
#
# The failure lands nowhere near the cause: the branch works perfectly in the worktree
# that created it, and fails in any other checkout as `Cannot find package 'three'`.
node_modules
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite/
# Per-worktree vite cache. `TC_VITE_CACHE_DIR` points here from tools/film.mjs and
# tools/qa-net.mjs, because every agent worktree symlinks node_modules at the shared checkout
# and vite's default cache is therefore one directory shared by as many vite processes as
# there are agents running a gate.
.vite-cache/
# Every raster format, not just PNG. This listed `*.png` alone, and a review agent
# writing JPEG comparison plates into `screenshots/` put frames derived from
# copyrighted press material onto a committable path. It caught itself; the next one
# might not.
screenshots/**/*.png
screenshots/**/*.jpg
screenshots/**/*.jpeg
screenshots/**/*.webp
screenshots/**/*.avif
# Video too, for the same reason and a bigger one: `tools/film-walleye.mjs` records the page
# with Playwright's own screencast and a thirty-second walk is six to ten megabytes of WebM.
# A camera pass writes four of them. Hand the files over; do not commit them.
screenshots/**/*.webm
screenshots/**/*.mp4
screenshots/**/report.json
# ...and the tagged variants: probe-plan writes `report-<tag>.json`, which the bare name misses.
screenshots/**/report-*.json
# `tools/film.mjs --out=screenshots/<dir>` puts its isolated Vite optimiser cache and its
# per-frame manifests inside the output directory, and neither is a raster so neither was
# caught by the list above. A film run into the repo staged ~20 committable copies of three.js
# before this line existed.
screenshots/**/.vite-cache/
screenshots/**/stills.json
screenshots/**/film.json
screenshots/**/cut.json
screenshots/**/.metadata_never_index
!screenshots/keep/**

# Local-only visual reference material. Copyrighted third-party screenshots used
# for side-by-side critique; never committed or redistributed.
reference/

# Crops CUT FROM reference/ are still the same copyrighted press material, just
# smaller. Same rule: local-only, never committed. The index.json alongside them
# is only coordinates and prose, but it is worthless without the images, so the
# whole directory goes.
reference-crops/

# Scratch renders of the reference plates (grid overlays, crop trials).
tools/scratch/.grid/
tools/scratch/.preview/
tools/scratch/.try/
